            <ArticleTitle>Fourteen years of severe arthralgia in a man without gastrointestinal symptoms: atypical Whipple's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>492-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/JCM.01833-08</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report here the case of Whipple's disease in a 60-year-old man with severe arthralgia and systemic disorders but without gastrointestinal manifestations. The patient had different clinical diagnoses over a period of 14 years. We identified Tropheryma whipplei by real-time PCR. Molecular typing was also performed by sequencing the 16S-23S rRNA intergenic spacer region and domain III of the 23S rRNA gene.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
